[[SECTION]]
UID: L2-ARCH-PRINCIPLES
TITLE: Key architecture principles

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Three to seven fundamental architectural decisions. These are the choices that
shape everything below, and the ones most often violated silently later - which
is why they carry IDs rather than sitting in a bullet list.
<<<

[ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLE]
UID: AP-01
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - One architectural decision, stated so a later design choice can be
checked against it. For example: separation of concerns between client and
backend; authentication delegated to the institutional system; payment
processing outsourced to a certified gateway; data held centrally and cached on
clients.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
TBD - Why this decision, and what the alternative would have cost.
<<<
IMPLICATIONS: >>>
TBD - What this rules out, so a reader knows when they are about to break it.
<<<
