[[SECTION]]
UID: L2-ARCH-DIAGRAM
TITLE: Architecture diagram

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The diagram should show every user type, software element, hardware element and
partner element; the primary interactions and data flows; the system boundary
between internal and external; and the major groupings or layers.

Mermaid equivalents for the recommended notation:

| Notation | Meaning | Mermaid |
|---|---|---|
| Rectangle | Software element | `SE01["SE-01 Name"]` |
| Cylinder | Database | `SE04[("SE-04 Name")]` |
| Stick figure | User type | `UT01(["UT-01 Name"])` |
| Dashed rectangle | Partner element | `PE01["PE-01 Name"]` + dashed link |
| Cloud / device | Hardware element | `HE01[/"HE-01 Name"/]` |
| Arrow | Data flow | `-->` |
| Dashed line | Partner boundary crossing | `-. label .->` |
| Grouping | Layer or boundary | `subgraph` |

Label every node with its element ID. A diagram whose boxes do not correspond
to identified elements cannot be checked against the text, and drifts.

```mermaid
graph TB
  UT01(["UT-01 TBD"]) --> SE01
  subgraph client["Client tier"]
    SE01["SE-01 TBD"]
  end
  subgraph app["Application tier"]
    SE02["SE-02 TBD"]
    SE04[("SE-04 TBD")]
  end
  SE01 --> SE02
  SE02 --> SE04
  SE02 -. "TBD" .-> PE01["PE-01 TBD"]
  SE02 --> HE01[/"HE-01 TBD"/]
```

Detailed interaction flows belong in system scenarios, not here.
<<<

