[[SECTION]]
UID: L2-ARCH-HARDWARE
TITLE: System elements - hardware elements

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The physical devices and infrastructure the software runs on. This is what gives
the reader a tangible sense of the system's physical presence.

`PROCUREMENT` must always be explicit: `Procurement-required` where something
must be bought, `Assumed-existing` where users or the institution already have
it, `Managed-service` where a provider supplies it. An unstated procurement
position is how hardware costs get discovered late.

Keep technical characteristics high-level - minimum OS versions, connectivity,
form factor, quantities. Processor and memory specifications belong in the
System Realization Concept.
<<<

[HARDWARE_ELEMENT]
UID: HE-01
PROCUREMENT: Assumed-existing
STATUS: Draft
MANAGED_BY: TBD
LOCATION: TBD
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - What this hardware is, its purpose, and who owns or manages it. Include
location where the hardware is fixed in place or where location affects the
design; omit it for portable user devices unless it matters.
<<<
RUNS: >>>
TBD - Which software elements run on this: [LINK: SE-01]
<<<
